From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dake2482 <dake2482@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:18:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: fit Ark K3.1 Pro's default temperature to thinking
 off

Reported by dake2482: ZCode through a routing group fails with an opaque
non-retryable turn error while the provider probe passes. Ark Coding Plan
rejects missing/null temperature when Magpie adds thinking disabled.

After thinking adaptation and extraBody, supply 0.6 only for the exact
Ark host and kimi-k3.1-pro model when disabled and temperature is absent
or null. Numeric extraBody overrides, enabled/default thinking, other
models/providers and token counting keep their behavior. The confirmed
!temperature=1 / !thinking=enabled workaround remains valid.

Verification on macOS arm64, Go 1.26.8, isolated HOME/XDG, pinned caches:
- 20 new wire-path cases pass; removing the final fix makes 10 fail with
  the captured 400. Focused sampling/extraBody/thinking regressions pass.
- New test passes -race -count=3. gofmt and diff --check are clean.
- macOS vet/build, Linux amd64 nogui vet/build, Windows amd64 vet/build
  pass (cross-platform CGO disabled).
- Full go test -tags nogui -timeout 45m ./... run: gateway passes in
  940.509s; six tests in four other packages fail, also on clean b596da7.
  GUI helper/proxy failures pass with a test-only scutil stand-in (#2562,
  #5749). Bun proxy/Git update failures pass with Bun 1.4.4 instead of
  PATH's 1.3.9 (#3397, #5419). All five pass together in controlled rerun.
  Library TestCodexOffKeepsAppsOwnConfig/imported remains textually red
  (#5749, #5822): inline TOML env vs original table; parsed node_repl
  maps are equal. Full suite is not claimed green.
- Built sandbox gateway + real Ark Coding Plan: original group shape,
  enabled thinking, disabled Chat/Responses and exact reporter override
  all return HTTP 200, complete streams and OK. Credential copies removed.

Not run: full race suite, browser tests (no GUI changes), native Linux
or Windows runtime, real other Ark plans. An initial full test invocation
with MAGPIE_NO_ACCOUNTS=1 suppressed fixture accounts; the full run above
was made after correcting that harness mistake.

Related: yetone/magpie#4495
