nxiang0010 on Discord): only a route above can make auto mode work there, and none of magpie's other routes can; the wiring turns the review off in its settings unless every model it can reach through magpie surely gets the results back (`AutoModeAnswered`: the subscription or `api.anthropic.com`, not a relay, which may drop them; `claudeReviewEnv`, [agent wiring](agent-wiring.md), JoyYoung2Lucky on X), which is the page's remedy for a gateway that can't run the checks (1EFLOPS on X: Codex's model behind magpie). Reviewed there means `AutoModeReviewable`: a reviewed model on a route that reaches the Messages API, since a Claude model asked on a relay's Chat or Responses URL is translated and never carries the review (nexnull on Discord, `TestAutoModeReviewableAsksOnMessages`).
